1305 0 obj
  << /ActualText (There are potential alternative interpretations of this behavior\054 however\054 that I have chosen to apply\056 The first I will call the \034Double\055Back\035 interpretation\054 where the rewind is an unbroken chain of causality\054 sufficiently driven in parallel spatial conditions \050though reversed\051 to the same point in time t\054 but along an almost negligibly different path\056 The causality c impacts the spatial and temporal state over successive c \075 c \053 1 steps\054 where causality is not synonymous with time t\056 Therefore the causal driver impacts the backwards movement along the time axis\054 without \034overwriting\035 the original path of causality that has been traversed\056 The state of the system up to the point of rewind appears close enough to the same\054 but is not in fact the same state which has already been trodden\056\n\n     \n)
     /K [ 75 ]
     /P 1306 0 R
     /Pg 1230 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
