1381 0 obj
  << /ActualText (cycles of behavior are not patterns we break free from after a single decision\054 a single effort\056 They are continuous processes which we must inflect attentively and minutely and consciously along each step of the path\054 until the system state gravitates to a different orbit\056 Conversely\054 just because you seem to find yourself in the same place does not mean you have not grown\056 It is not the same place\054 and you are not the same person\056 You can\031t go home again\054 but also you don\031t have to\056 The system state at time t will progress to a different state at t\0531 than it progressed to on a previous orbit\056)
     /K [ 151 ]
     /P 1382 0 R
     /Pg 1230 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

